    "done_when": "A report at ~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s21-boundary-two-trees-measured.md, under 40 KB, takes the-boundary-check-reads-two-trees §2's measure from runs promoted at heads that descend from merge 1859c0d19, the two-tree supervisor. It covers at least three fenced runs and at least one unfenced run, read from their ledger rows under docs/state/reckon/runs/ and their run directories (tree-snapshot.json, the supervisor and promotion records). For each run it gives: the run id, whether the launch plan composed a fence (from the run's own composed plan, not the FENCE_WORKERS constant), the registered worktree count at dispatch, the number of trees its supervisor snapshot read, the number of trees promotion's boundary check read, and the wall time from dispatch to worker start and from crew complete's start to its commit, where the records hold them. It compares those figures with the same figures for at least three fenced runs promoted before 1859c0d19. It states §2's falsifier verdict: whether at least three fenced runs at the merged head each read 2 trees against a registered count above 100, whether an unfenced run in the same window read the full count, and whether any run read 2 trees while its plan composed no fence, naming that run if so. Tree count is the primary figure, and timings are reported with the caveat that filesystem load moves them. It includes one figure, a per-run bar of trees read against registered trees before and after, at ~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s21-boundary-two-trees-measured.svg beside the report, with no gridlines, despined axes and direct labels. No repository file changes. Every command and its output is logged under the run directory, ending EXIT=.",
